{"advisories": [{"file": "starlette/middleware/body_limit.py", "line": 38, "pass": 1, "severity": "advisory", "text": "The Content-Length fail-fast is lazy: it runs on the first receive() or the response start, not when the request arrives. An app that does side effects before reading or responding is not stopped early. This is a deliberate trade-off to let inner limits override the outer one, but it is not documented."}, {"file": "tests/test_body_limit.py", "line": 1, "pass": 2, "severity": "advisory", "text": "No test combines max_body_size with user middleware that wraps receive (for example BaseHTTPMiddleware), or checks websocket scopes through Starlette(max_body_size=...). Middleware-level pass-through for a non-http scope is tested."}, {"file": "tests/middleware/test_body_limit.py", "line": 78, "pass": 4, "severity": "advisory", "text": "collect_http returns a tuple whose second element is always None and is never used, so it can return just the sent list."}], "at": "2026-10-14T15:30:44+00:00", "attempt": 1, "event": "GateEvaluated", "failures": [], "gate": "review.approved", "passed": true, "run_id": "20261014T152342Z-fc8ea6", "schema_version": 1, "task": "T1", "verdict": "approve"}
